@startuml
hide empty members


class Database #lightgreen


interface GUI #lightsalmon
GUI ...> ItemListService


interface ItemListInterface #lightblue

class ItemListBuilder #lightblue
ItemListBuilder ..> ConcreteItemList: <<create>>

class ConcreteItemList #lightblue
ConcreteItemList --|> AbstractItemList: <<implement>>

class ItemBuilder #lightblue
ItemBuilder ..> AbstractItem: <<create>>

abstract class AbstractItem #lightblue
AbstractItem .l.o AbstractItemList
AbstractItem -- Unit

class Repository #khaki
Repository ..> Database
Repository ..> ConcreteItemList: <<store \n& load>>

' This will be two services actually:
'   RecipeService
'   ShoppingListService
' Since this would drastically reduce readability of the diagram those two services will both be
' presented by "ItemListService"
class ItemListService #plum {
}
ItemListService ..> ItemListInterface
ItemListService ..> ItemListBuilder
ItemListService ..> Repository
ItemListService ..> ItemBuilder
note right of ItemListService: This will be two services: \nRecipeService & ShoppingListService \nSince this would drastically reduce readability of the diagram, \nthose two services will both be presented by: "ItemListService"

abstract class AbstractItemList #lightblue
AbstractItemList .l.|> ItemListInterface
AbstractItemList -- Quantity

class Quantity #lightblue
Quantity o.r. Unit

class Unit #lightblue
legend bottom right
| **Color**         | **Layer**             |
| <#lightgreen>     | Database layer        |
| <#khaki>          | Repository layer      |
| <#lightblue>      | Application layer     |
| <#lightsalmon>    | Presentation layer    |
| <#plum>           | Service layer         |
end legend
@enduml

# Decisions
Language and Framework:
Laguage that is going to be used mainly in this project is kotlin.
This is a fast growing modern language, that runs on most operating systems and us fun to use.
Pros:
- Fun language
- Easy to read
- Cross platform
Cons:
- Small community -> fewer support
- High learning curve

The framework that is going to be used for this project is Compose multiplatform.
With this it should be possible to run a graphical user interface (GUI)
on most platforms and maybe even web in future as well.
Pros:
- Cross platform
- Web in Beta
Contra:
- Web in Beta
- Small community -> fewer support

# Authentication:
Firebender is going to be the choice for Authentication.

